Q.sejm_list_internal_score = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left opens talks over the legal form of its October list";
!}

= August 2023 — Five percent or eight?

A party committee clears **5%**, but its host controls nominations and the
public subsidy. We can instead ask separate parties to create a coalition
committee: each keeps its identity and a claim on funding, but all of us must
clear **8%**. The safer threshold therefore comes with the hardest terms.

The talks can include KO and the democratic parties, Third Way or one of its
hosts, PiS, independent Razem and compatible minor-left breakaways. A revived
SLD will not return through Razem, and PPS insists on its own committee if it
has already left.

